  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "RNA multiprofile scvi_n200 is currently the strongest direction (accuracy ~0.65, F1 ~0.63), but image-only ResNet50 singleprofile is weak (accuracy 0.208, F1 0.172), leaving uncertainty about whether image can contribute at all or whether the poor score is due to singleprofile/no aggregation. config_011 keeps the image encoder fixed and adds multiprofile avgpool, directly testing the profile/aggregation effect for image without introducing RNA or fusion. This is a minimal, high-information step before committing to multimodal ResNet50 fusion: if image improves, multimodal becomes more attractive; if not, ResNet50-based multimodal can be deprioritized."
}

